cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this note, please cite it as below."
title: "A Shorter Route to Tao's Almost-Bounded-Orbits Theorem via a Polylogarithmic Fourier Input"
authors:
  - family-names: Humphrey
    given-names: Nathan
type: article
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Tao's theorem that almost all Collatz orbits attain almost bounded values rests on
  superpolynomial decay of the characteristic function of the Syracuse random variable.
  This note shows that a polylogarithmic input, Phi(n) << n^(-1/4) (log n)^(-3/2-delta),
  already suffices, and supplies it using only Cases 1-2 of Tao's section 7 induction.
  It is a simplification of Tao's proof, not a new result about the Collatz map.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - Syracuse random variable
  - Fourier decay
  - almost bounded orbits
